A||N||9||turbo86se||Weird Noise from rear wheel||||5||
Z||000000||turbo86se||05-25-2000||04:40 PM||||<BR>hey everyone. Today I took my 86SE for a quick spin after I installed the spoiler, and I noticed a squeaky noise from my rear left wheel. I just installed new 16" wheels and tires, and haven't noticed the noise before. Is it possible I overtightened the lug nuts? The noise is noticeable at low speeds. Now I'm kinda nervous driving the car!<BR>If it wasn't so humid I'd put the old 14" wheel on just to see what happens. It's only 100 degrees in Myrtle Beach!!<BR>TIA     -joel||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||05-25-2000||05:06 PM||||Over tightening shouldn't be a problem (unless you break the stud off  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) Defientely check for UNDERtightening though!<P>Also, check for clearance problems. The tire could be barely rubbing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||05-25-2000||05:06 PM||||<BR>You sure it's not the brake wear indicator scrapping the rotor?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||05-25-2000||05:38 PM||||Is it possible that the lug nuts were unevenly tightened?  <BR>The rotors were turned 1000 miles ago, and the brake pads all around are brand new. The tires are 225/50/16,  if they're rubbing, how can I tell and what do I look for?<BR>Thanks guys!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||triker||05-25-2000||06:30 PM||||You might check the gravel shield behind the rotor. They can be bent when pulling a wheel off and will rub against the rotor. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fret Naught||05-25-2000||09:37 PM||||That's my guess, the brake dust shield is rubbing, easy fis if that is the case, bend it back a bit. If the tire is rubbing, it will show up as wear real quick.||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||05-25-2000||10:36 PM||||Thanks for the help everyone, I bent back the shield everywhere I could visibly see the shield, and in between thunderstorms, I took her out. The first few minutes, everything was great. As I'm pulling into my neighborhood, I heard it again. You know the engine noise you get in your stereo thru your speakers? That's what it was like, only coming by the rear wheel. If I accellerate, the pitch get higher. There's also another "frumping" sound too. Something must be rubbing somewhere, it's rotational. HELP!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||05-29-2000||10:06 PM||||turbo... hows the sound?  you know, ive been getting something like that, since i got my car driveable, and i suspect a couple of things.<P>either its the bearings going bad, or the half shaft needs to be lubed.  either way, the noize from these will be rotational.<P>also, just curious, whatis the condition of your parking brake cables?  i am also thinking this could have some affect on both of our problems.<P>as for lose lug nuts... they should be torqued to 80lbs.  <P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000008||turbo86se||05-29-2000||10:49 PM||||Hey hoop, <BR>My mechanic was over today installing a new A/C compressor, so now my A/C blows COLD. We took it for a drive and we noticed the noise. At first he thought it may be the bearing, but then we noticed the steel-braided brake line was rubbing the wheel, making the noise. Hasn't happened since. If you looked on the tire you could see where it was rubbing.<BR>Thanks for the specs on the lug nuts, I was wandering about that!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>See you in a couple weeks? (Williamsburg)||||reg||1
Z||000009||bHooper||05-30-2000||06:47 AM||||your welcome.<P>as for Williamsburge, i still have a lot of work to do to make my car trip worthy.<P>and i also have a lot of projects to catch up on around the house to  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>we'll see...||||reg||1
